WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:02.821
(dramatic music)

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:05.940
- [Narrator] Here are five differences

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.363
between the Mortal Engines books and film.

00:00:09.306 --> 00:00:11.610
(sorrowful music)

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.420
Fans love Philip Reeve's
sci-fi quartet of books,

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.760
which have been adapted to
screen by Peter Jackson.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.670
But did you notice these five alterations?

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.170
One, Hester's scar.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.520
Fans have commented
that heroine Hester Shaw

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.580
has a dramatically
reduced scar in the film.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.410
The character you recognize from the books

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.630
looks a little different on screen.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.630
- Okay, Hester's scar is a digital scar.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.440
We did have a silicone
prosthetic that was designed,

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.510
which we shot her through the whole film.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:44.370
But it just wasn't impactful enough.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.500
It doesn't have the actual
depth that we needed.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.830
And the only way you can get that,

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.830
because with a prosthetic, you
can only actually build up.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.980
The only way to actually eat into the skin

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.790
is to cut them or to actually use

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.970
a chemical called collodion,

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:03.830
which was used extensively
in the old days.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.250
It was really bad for your skin, too,

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.347
and we're not allowed to use it anymore.

00:01:06.347 --> 00:01:08.830
And it was used in Tom
Beringer in Platoon.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.510
It actually shrinks your skin.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.280
You paint it on, so we
couldn't do that, not to Hera.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.613
- [Narrator] Two, St. Paul's Cathedral.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.400
The book features giant traction cities,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.313
one of which was based on London.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.990
- There's no one traction
city can look like the other.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.240
- Yeah, and they also have to be

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.420
believable in their own
world so if it's Saltzahken,

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.310
then it's a mining town
that's scraping salt off

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:36.160
and it should look like it's
a town that can scrape salt.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.140
- So we flipped St. Paul's around.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.550
If you actually look
at the teaser trailer,

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.300
St. Paul's is actually

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.080
the orientation of the
doors facing forward.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.720
It's this thing in the
book where there's a statue

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.060
of one of the gods Clio.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:55.940
And Clio is always reaching
back into the past,

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.350
so she's facing backwards.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.180
And so we wanted London to have this...

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.040
It's moving forward, but then everything

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.240
is sort of more facing the back,

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.570
the wind tunnel effect.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.483
- [Narrator] Three, Minions.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.520
In the books, Disney
characters are prayed to

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.713
in the futuristic London museum.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.540
But as the film is produced by Universal,

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.633
these have been changed to Minions.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.663
Four, Shrike.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.620
The characterisation of Stalker Shrike

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.933
is one of the best things about the film.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.400
Actor Stephen Lang, who you
might recognize from Avatar,

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.200
brought some unusual
influences to the role

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.720
to make him look a little different.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.080
- Shrike is described in the book,

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.110
he's got quite big proportions

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.280
and he's a bit more robotic.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.770
And we just worked out

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.780
the more human we made his proportions,

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.450
he felt more sympathetic.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.790
Stephen sort of looked at different birds,

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.950
'cause the Shrike bird is
actually the butcher bird.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.180
He was sort of looking at some stuff

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.510
that Rudolf Nureyev did for Swan Lake

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.050
and how he would move like a
bird and not move his arms.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.620
It would be very easy for
him to feel Terminator-esque

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.220
or have some kind of locomotion

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.950
that made him feel slightly awkward

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.400
and so it gave him a grace.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.083
- [Narrator] Five, Anna Fang.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.440
Jihae Kim stars as Anna Fang in the movie.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.030
You might know her as a
badass character in the books,

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.463
but they have really
stepped it up in the movie.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:29.960
- Fang being such a
strong, empowered character

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.383
with such complexities, it was,

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.153
it was a gift.

00:03:34.153 --> 00:03:35.210
It was a gift to be able to play her.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:38.930
It actually helped me
get empowered myself, so.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.830
- [Narrator] To become leader
of the Anti-Traction League,

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.700
she worked with Mark Trotter,

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.613
who is a nine times world
champion of taekwondo.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.810
Fans will be pleased that her true name

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.163
is revealed in the film.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.470
- Anna Fang has another name,

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.876
which we managed to get
that reference in there

00:03:57.876 --> 00:04:00.360
and sort of a little bit of an explanation

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.150
about where it came from.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:03.560
- [Narrator] Tell us in the comments below

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.655
if you spotted anything that we didn't.

00:04:05.655 --> 00:04:08.405
(dramatic music)

